/-!
# The unique maximal 2-local case: Sections 2.1–2.3

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, *The Classification of Quasithin Groups*, combined
manuscript (1 March 2004), pp. 518–527.

The chapter studies a simple QTKE group whose Sylow 2-subgroup lies in a
unique maximal 2-local subgroup `M`. Section 2.2 treats the empty-δ case
by Bender-group recognition; Section 2.3 constructs and studies local
subgroups in Γ₀ for the remaining case.

The elementary normalizer, Sylow and finite selection arguments are
re-exported here. Lemma 2.2.3 now puts the literal fusion family in S₂e,
so empty δ constructs the full local-control witness. Transfer excludes
index-two subgroups of M and of its actual surjective action images.
The source local transitivity also rules out three commuting conjugate
components: their cyclic lifts give odd rank three in an actual two-local.
The projected splitting, component balance and Bender-model action facts
still require their independent source theorems before full recognition.
-/
